<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simraungadh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Simraongarh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simraungadh is a town and archaeological site in Bara District of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, close to the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>. It was the capital of the Karnat dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithila">Mithila</a> from the late 11th century until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghiyath-al-din-tughluq">Ghiyath al-Din Tughluq</a> took it in 1324. Remains of its walls, tanks and temples survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simraungadh.jpg" alt="Simraungadh" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scyfie · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jharokhar_Pokhari_Simroungarh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
